INSERT INTO feature VALUES('declaration-account','editor','The per-declaration account','language-server','partial','ordinary',NULL,'The session keeps one row for each declaration of the latest judged revision, by the content key that the declaration''s incremental checkpoint holds: the checker''s verdict, the kernel tier and the compile tier. A judgement keeps the kernel tier of each declaration whose key and verdict are unchanged, so an edit to a comment or to another declaration moves no row. The admission then writes each row again. A withheld tier names its support by position, so a judgement sets it back to pending. At the counts layer each row also holds what the engine did for the declaration in the latest recheck: the hits and the misses of the checker''s memo, the arena nodes, the molded forms, the obligations, whether the incremental pass judged it and whether it crossed, and the goals of the kernel''s check that the kernel recalled, expanded and kept. At the timings layer each row also keeps the last 32 samples of the declaration''s judgement and of its admission, each a wall and an allocation count, and the account keeps the same rings for each phase of the document; a ring folds to its p50 and its p99. The render bus carries the account as one card per declaration, keyed by its content: the whole list at the attach and at a resync, then the edits that drop and put cards by key, and nothing for a list that did not change. The compile column waits on the hub''s emitter, and the attested verdict cache''s tier waits on the cache.','surface-session core-incremental surface-lsp surface-render-remote','crates/surface-session/tests/account.rs crates/surface-session/tests/counts.rs crates/surface-session/tests/timings.rs crates/core-incremental/src/checkpoint/tests.rs crates/surface-lsp/src/server.rs crates/surface-lsp/src/hub.rs crates/surface-render-remote/src/account.rs','crate-tests','#6272 #2797');
